From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: cap SPI NOR frequency on ROCK Pi 4B

ROCK Pi 4B uses the same SPI NOR design as ROCK Pi 4A. On ROCK Pi 4A,
108 MHz selects an 18.56 MHz SCLK, and bulk reads return corrupt data.
flashcp then fails verification. 10 MHz selects 9.28 MHz and is stable.

Apply the ROCK Pi 4A value to ROCK Pi 4B. Not tested on a ROCK Pi 4B.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4b.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4b.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4b.dts
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ &spi1 {
 	flash@0 {
 		compatible = "jedec,spi-nor";
 		reg = <0>;
-		spi-max-frequency = <108000000>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <10000000>;
 	};
 };
 
